{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T20:37:32.127Z","data":{"text":"Done. Implemented capability group lanes in the graph and wrote the result file.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n- `src/core/web/web-data-types.ts` — `WebCapabilityNode` gains `group?: string | null`.\n- `src/core/web/web-data-graph.ts` — fills `group` from `readLivingSidecar` (null on missing/malformed sidecar).\n- `packages/ui/src/graph/types.ts` — added `GraphGroupHeader`, `groups` on `GraphLayout`, and `groupHeaderHeight` geometry.\n- `packages/ui/src/graph/layout.ts` — groups lanes by name (ungrouped last, original order within group), reserves header rows, returns header positions; no-group case matches the old layout.\n- `packages/ui/src/graph/GraphCanvas.tsx` — draws one labelled header row per group, none without groups.\n- `tests/ui-graph-groups.test.tsx` — new tests for grouped ordering/headers, unchanged ungrouped layout, canvas rendering, and the web data sidecar cases.\n\n**Verification:** task verify passes (6/6); `pnpm verify` exits 0 (2586 CLI tests, 94 UI tests, lint, both typechecks, build).\n\n**Note:** `group` is optional rather than required, because the existing out-of-scope `tests/ui-graph.test.tsx` and `tests/ui-report.test.tsx` capability literals must pass unchanged; derived nodes always set it. Documented under `## Deviated` in `openspec/changes/105-capability-sidecar/.run/results/6.md`."}}
